  # Terminal-wrapped links

  Render this document with OSC8 off and a zero right margin to check
  contiguous URL bytes and natural terminal wrapping. Words after each URL
  should resume at the correct column, then wrap normally with the configured
  left margin.

  Click detection also depends on the terminal and multiplexer. For tmux, use
  OSC8 on with a supporting terminal and tmux's hyperlinks feature enabled.
  The no-OSC8 goldens verify URL bytes and layout; mouse-click handling
  belongs to the terminal and multiplexer.

  The example.com addresses below are rendering examples, not live
  documentation pages.

  ## Paragraph

  Read the long report
  (https://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstration
  /keeping-the-entire-destination-clickable?session=0123456789abcdef0123456789
  abcdef&source=golden) and then keep reading this sentence. These words
  should fill the space left on the terminal row before the next ordinary line
  break.

  ## Bare URL

  https://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstration/
  keeping-the-entire-destination-clickable?
  session=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef&source=golden followed by ordinary
  words that should still wrap normally after the address.

  ## Angle-bracket autolink

  https://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstration…
  followed by another sentence. Its placement should use the cursor reached
  after the terminal wraps the URL.

  ## Lists

  - Read the same long report
    (https://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstrati
    on/keeping-the-entire-destination-clickable?session=0123456789abcdef012345
    6789abcdef&source=golden). The URL continuation rows should contain no
    inserted list indentation. These following words should wrap normally.
  - A second item confirms that the usual list indentation returns after the
    link-containing item.

  1. An ordered item with a parenthesized citation
     (https://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstrat
     ion/keeping-the-entire-destination-clickable?session=0123456789abcdef0123
     456789abcdef&source=golden) and enough following text to exercise another
     ordinary line break.
  2. The next ordered item should retain its normal marker and indentation.

  ## Quoted list

  > - A quote containing the long report
  >   (https://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstra
  >   tion/keeping-the-entire-destination-clickable?session=0123456789abcdef01
  >   23456789abcdef&source=golden). The address must not gain quote markers
  >   or spaces between its bytes. The text after it should wrap normally.
  > - The next quoted item should regain its normal quote and list prefixes.

  ## Bare hostname

  www.terminal-wrap-demonstration-with-a-long-hostname.that-still-has-valid-le
  ngth-dns-labels.example.com followed by ordinary words. The same cursor
  accounting should work for an address without an explicit scheme.

  ## Scheme-relative address

  //localhost/abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz a b c d e f

  - //localhost/abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv a b c d e f

  //abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv a b c d e f

  ## Styled addresses

  https://example.com/abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz a b c d e f

  https://example.com/abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz. a b c d e f

  https://example.com/abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz a b c d e f

  ## Parentheses inside a destination

  David Teece's Profiting from Technological Innovation
  (https://doi.org/10.1016/0048-7333(86)90027-2) keeps the full DOI, including
  its parentheses. This final sentence should wrap normally too.
